=== DESIGN ===

Existing tesla.Client surface (read from
internal/tesla/client_vehicle_data.go and internal/tesla/types.go):

  func (c *Client) GetVehicleData(ctx context.Context, vin string,
      endpoints ...string) (*VehicleDataResponse, error)

    Returns ErrVehicleAsleep on 408/504 (Request Timeout / Gateway
    Timeout), ErrRateLimited on 429, generic "status %d" error on any
    other non-200, ErrUnauthorized on 401 (via the client's
    underlying doRequest -> apiResponse path).

  type VehicleDataResponse struct {
      ID, VehicleID int64
      VIN, DisplayName, State string
      ChargeState, ClimateState, DriveState,
      VehicleState, VehicleConfig (typed structs)
  }

REALITY-CHECK NOTE: VehicleDataResponse does NOT currently include a
`gui_settings` block (we ran `grep -n 'gui|Gui|GUI' internal/tesla/`
and matched only this design log's narrative). The prompt assumes
gui_settings is reachable through *tesla.Client; in practice the
typed response throws gui_settings away during json.Unmarshal because
no Go field is tagged for it. This package therefore CANNOT call
client.GetVehicleData and harvest gui_settings — the data simply does
not survive the typed decode.

Two mutually-exclusive ways to satisfy the prompt's intent without
violating the gate's "no http.* in bootstrap.go" rule:

  (a) Modify internal/tesla/types.go to add a GuiSettings field, then
      have bootstrap.go call client.GetVehicleData(...) and read it.
      REJECTED — types.go is OUTSIDE the allowed-files allowlist
      ("internal/tesla/bootstrap/" + the log only). Touching it would
      trigger the gate's git-status drift check (gate covenant 9).

  (b) Define an interface seam in this package — VehicleDataClient —
      whose method returns the four gui_settings fields as a typed
      DTO. Bootstrapper holds the interface (NOT *tesla.Client),
      tests substitute a recording fake, and the production wiring
      (a future prompt — phase-42-0030+) implements the adapter that
      wraps *tesla.Client and pulls gui_settings from the raw
      response bytes (e.g. via a new GetVehicleDataRaw or a
      GuiSettings struct added in that future migration).

Path (b) is what the prompt itself instructs in its tests section —
"table tests with a fake `tesla.Client` (interface seam)" — so we
adopt it. The Bootstrapper.client field's declared type is the
interface; the doc comment cites Client for production wiring.

Interface seam (this package):

  type VehicleDataClient interface {
      // FetchGuiSettings retrieves the four wire-format unit
      // preferences from /api/1/vehicles/{vehicleID}/vehicle_data.
      // Errors MUST be one of:
      //   - ErrTransient: 408/429/503/5xx — Bootstrapper retries.
      //   - ErrUnauthorized: 401/403 — Bootstrapper returns it
      //     immediately so the caller can re-auth.
      //   - any other non-nil err: returned as-is, no retry.
      FetchGuiSettings(ctx context.Context, vehicleID int64) (GuiSettings, error)
  }

  type GuiSettings struct {
      DistanceUnits     string    // "mi/hr" or "km/hr"
      TemperatureUnits  string    // "F" or "C"
      TirePressureUnits string    // "Psi" or "Bar"
      ChargeRateUnits   string    // "mi/hr" or "km/hr"
      Now               time.Time // optional response timestamp
  }

This decouples the bootstrap orchestration (retry, mapping, write)
from the concrete REST decoding. Tests inject a fake; production
wiring will adapt *tesla.Client in a separate prompt without
re-touching this package.

GUI-SETTINGS → (Kind, ActiveUnit) MAPPING TABLE
(case-insensitive trim; defaults are NOT inferred — an unrecognised
value is a hard error so we never silently corrupt a US car):

  gui_distance_units:
    "mi/hr" | "mi"        -> KindDistance, ActiveUnitMiles
    "km/hr" | "km"        -> KindDistance, ActiveUnitKilometers

  gui_temperature_units:
    "F"                   -> KindTemperature, ActiveUnitFahrenheit
    "C"                   -> KindTemperature, ActiveUnitCelsius

  gui_tirepressure_units:
    "Psi"                 -> KindPressure, ActiveUnitPSI
    "Bar"                 -> KindPressure, ActiveUnitBar

  gui_charge_rate_units:
    "mi/hr" | "mi"        -> KindCharge, ActiveUnitDistance
    "km/hr" | "km"        -> KindCharge, ActiveUnitDistance
    "%"                   -> KindCharge, ActiveUnitPercent
    NOTE: Tesla emits gui_charge_rate_units as a distance unit string
    (mi/hr or km/hr) when the user prefers range display, and "%"
    when the user prefers percent. The wire-format itself does not
    carry the percent variant via gui_charge_rate_units in current
    fleet-telemetry releases, but the mapping is symmetric for
    forward-compatibility.

Source for ALL bootstrap writes: unithistory.SourceRESTBootstrap.

EFFECTIVE_FROM: GuiSettings.Now (UTC) if non-zero, else time.Now()
captured at the moment of the SUCCESSFUL REST call. Subtract a
1-second buffer ("the snapshot represents *current* prefs as of
fetch time") so any subsequent telemetry sample at instant t finds
this bootstrap row via the "ORDER BY effective_from DESC, id DESC
LIMIT 1 WHERE effective_from <= t" lookup in unit_history.At.

RETRY POLICY
The prompt's prose contains a minor self-inconsistency ("schedule a
single retry with exponential backoff (max 3 attempts: 1s, 5s, 30s)"
— "single" vs "max 3" vs three explicit backoffs). Resolution:
  - Max 3 attempts (1 initial + 2 retries) — honors "max 3 attempts".
  - Backoffs between attempts: [1s, 5s] — the wait BEFORE attempts
    2 and 3.
  - 30s is the per-attempt context.WithTimeout deadline so a single
    hung REST call cannot stall startup beyond 30+5+30+1+30 ~= 96s
    worst case (still well under any reasonable startup budget).
  - The metric tesla_bootstrap_skipped_total{vehicle_id, reason} is
    incremented EXACTLY ONCE per Seed call when retries are
    exhausted (matches the prompt's "exhausts retries before
    returning nil"). reason is one of: vehicle_asleep, rate_limited,
    transient, unknown.
  - All three numeric values from the prompt (1s, 5s, 30s) are
    consumed (two as backoffs, one as per-attempt timeout) so no
    intent is dropped.

Configurable for tests via Option-pattern fields on Bootstrapper:
  now      func() time.Time          // default time.Now
  sleep    func(context.Context, time.Duration) error
  backoffs []time.Duration           // default [1s, 5s]
  perAttemptTimeout time.Duration    // default 30s

ERROR TAXONOMY (this package)
  ErrTransient    — caller's REST returned 408/429/503/5xx; retry.
  ErrUnauthorized — caller's REST returned 401/403; return to caller.
  ErrBadGuiSettings — REST returned 200 but a gui_settings string
                      was unrecognised; bootstrap returns this so
                      operations sees a clear schema-drift signal.

PROMETHEUS METRIC
  Namespace=tesla, Subsystem=bootstrap, Name=skipped_total
  Fully qualified: tesla_bootstrap_skipped_total
  Labels: vehicle_id (string form of int64), reason
  Cardinality concern: vehicle_id is unbounded across a fleet. The
  prompt explicitly requires this label so an operator can identify
  WHICH vehicles are unprotected (per Decision 9e in ADR-004:
  telemetry without unit context is dropped). For a 100-vehicle
  install the cardinality is trivial; the runbook (Prompt 0090)
  documents alert thresholds.

=== UNIT_TEST ===

Tests use a fakeRepo (pure in-memory, mirrors the unit_history.Repo
contract) and a fakeClient (pure in-memory, returns canned
GuiSettings or canned errors) so the suite has zero external deps.

Test cases:
  TestSeed_PerKindVariant_*    — table tests for every supported
                                 string-to-(Kind,ActiveUnit) mapping;
                                 asserts 4 Record calls with the
                                 right Entry values and source
                                 SourceRESTBootstrap.
  TestSeed_TransientRetryExhausted
                                 — fakeClient always returns
                                 ErrTransient; assert exactly 3
                                 attempts, metric incremented
                                 exactly once with the right labels,
                                 final return is nil (so startup
                                 is never blocked).
  TestSeed_AuthErrorImmediate   — fakeClient returns ErrUnauthorized
                                 on attempt 1; assert exactly 1
                                 attempt, metric NOT incremented,
                                 ErrUnauthorized propagated.
  TestSeed_Idempotent_RowCount4 — call Seed twice in succession;
                                 assert fakeRepo holds exactly 4
                                 rows (one per kind) — second Seed
                                 is a no-op via Repo.Record's
                                 ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING contract.
  TestSeed_BadGuiSettings       — REST succeeds but a unit string is
                                 garbage; assert ErrBadGuiSettings
                                 propagated, no rows written, metric
                                 not incremented.
  TestSeed_ContextCancelled     — ctx cancelled mid-backoff; assert
                                 ctx.Err() returned, metric NOT
                                 incremented.

Determinism: fake sleep is a no-op (returns immediately) so the
suite runs in milliseconds without sleeping the real 6+ seconds.

